$VER: analog.acepansion 1.0 (18.05.2026) "Analog Joystick ACEpansion"

Analog Joystick ACEpansion
===========================

Plugin for ACE CPC Emulator which provides analog joystick support
for the Amstrad CPC/GX4000, based on the Tennis Cup 2 cartridge's
analog joystick routine.

  https://www.cpcwiki.eu/index.php/Tennis_Cup_2_(cartridge)

Description
-----------
The GX4000/Plus range includes ADC (Analog-to-Digital Converter)
hardware that allows reading analog joystick position. Tennis Cup 2
is the only known game to support this feature, converting the analog
signals to digital directions via software.

This ACEpansion exposes the ADC hardware to emulated CPC/GX4000
systems, allowing analog joystick input in your own programs.

How It Works
------------
The ADC provides two channels:
  - Channel 0: X-axis (joystick left/right)
  - Channel 1: Y-axis (joystick up/down)

Raw ADC values range from 00h to 3Fh (0-63), with center at 1Fh (31).
The driver applies a dead zone of +/-13h around center, using the
same algorithm as Tennis Cup 2:

  +14h to +20h  -> direction (right or down)
  -14h to -1Fh  -> opposite  (left or up)
  -13h to +13h  -> dead zone (no direction)

The fire button is read from digital joystick 1 (keyboard row 9),
matching Tennis Cup 2's approach of analog directions + digital fire.

Installation
------------
Copy the contents of the Analog archive to your ACE directory.
Launch ACE using the ACE-Analog icon.

Settings
--------
Open the Analog Settings panel from the Plugins menu to configure:

  Joystick Port:
    Select which joystick port the analog stick is on.
    Default is port 1.

Z80 Driver
----------
The driver/analog_driver.asm file contains a complete Z80 assembly
driver for reading the analog joystick. It assembles with RASM:

  https://www.cpcwiki.eu/index.php/Tennis_Cup_2_(cartridge)

Key routines:

  CALL &A000 - analog_init:
    Initialize the driver and AY PSG for joystick reading.

  CALL &A003 - analog_read:
    Read ADC channels 0 and 1, convert to digital directions,
    and read fire button state. Updates the variable area.

Variables (PEEK from BASIC):

  PEEK(&A006) - joy_state:
    Combined joystick state bits:
      bit 0 = up, bit 1 = down
      bit 2 = left, bit 3 = right
      bit 4 = fire

  PEEK(&A007) - joy_x_raw:
    Raw ADC X-axis value (00h-3Fh)

  PEEK(&A008) - joy_y_raw:
    Raw ADC Y-axis value (00h-3Fh)

  PEEK(&A009) - joy_fire:
    Fire button state (0=released, non-0=pressed)

